		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4276&amp;p=32350#p32350"><![CDATA[
In order not to spoil the programming cable, you can make an adapter from a faulty USB cable and a USB socket. Remove the micro USB connector and solder it by swapping D+ and D-. There will be one programming cable for both 1701/1801 and TYT.<br><br>+5V can not be soldered. He is not needed. Do not forget to isolate the bitten off +5V wire well. A short circuit to the screen may occur.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1432">EU1AEQ</a> — Mon Jul 29, 2024 6:10 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
